/* SPDX-License-Identifier: proprietary */
/*
 * 0x130  ACU_soc -- pack state of charge, 0..100 %.
 *
 * 0xFF is the "no trustworthy estimate" sentinel (ams::soc::Unknown), NOT a
 * real reading: consumers must treat it as "unknown" rather than clamping it
 * to 100. It appears before the first OCV anchor and whenever the current
 * sensor faults or goes stale, since Coulomb counting cannot be trusted across
 * an unmeasured interval.
 *
 * Mirrors ams::acu_tx::encode_soc(). TELEMETRY ONLY -- nothing in the safety
 * path produces or consumes this value.
 *
 * 250 ms to match config::EcuSlowTxMs, the group tx_soc() actually rides in
 * (acu_can_task.cpp, alongside 0x136/0x137). This was declared 1000 ms when the
 * message landed while the scheduler sent it at 250 -- so the DBC told every
 * consumer 1 Hz while the AMS transmitted at 4 Hz. Harmless on the wire (one
 * extra byte-sized frame 3x/s on a 500 kbps bus) but wrong in the file other
 * teams import as the contract, and it would mis-size any receive timeout
 * derived from GenMsgCycleTime. If tx_soc() is ever moved to another cadence
 * group, this number moves with it.
 */

CAN_MSG(ACU_soc, 0x130, 1, "AMS", 250)
    FIELD_BE (soc_percent, uint8_t, 0, 8, 1, 0, "%")
CAN_MSG_END(ACU_soc)
